  way_eyebrow: "The Should way",
  way_h2: "GTD asks \"what's the next action?\" Should asks \"who does it?\"",
  way_p1: "Getting Things Done was built for one person keeping their own lists. Should is built for one person with a staff. Most things that come in never reach you: an agent handles them. You see only the steps that need your hands or your decision.",
  way_p2: "<b>Capture → Clarify → Route → Organize → Review → Engage.</b> Things come in on their own: calls, texts, mail, email. Agents work out what each one is and who should act on it. You check in with the morning text each day and a short sit-down each week.",
  way_rules: [
   ["Agent first", "Your attention is the scarce resource. If an agent can do it, or do all of it but one step, it does."],
   ["One-way and two-way doors", "Easy-to-undo calls, like wording, scheduling or a draft, agents just make and tell you in one line. Only hard-to-undo ones (money, sending, deleting for good, settings) come to you, once, named for what's at stake and with one recommendation."],
   ["Dates only for real deadlines", "Your calendar holds what has to happen on a day: appointments, deadlines. Nothing else."],
   ["Agents do the waiting", "Waiting on a reply, a refund or a package is the agents' job, and you can see the list anytime."],
   ["Fewer, better", "A short list you'll finish beats a long one you won't. Fewer things in flight at once."],
   ["Rest is part of the system", "Sundays are for rest. The staff plans around it."],
  ],
  way_p3: "A staff role, the Philosopher, looks after the Should way. It reads widely, keeps the ideas worth borrowing and proposes new ones. You decide which get tried.",

  rules_eyebrow: "The ground rules",
  rules_h2: "They work for you, not the other way around",
  rules: [
   ["Nothing happens without your yes", "Nothing gets bought, sent, booked or deleted until you approve that exact thing. They fill the cart; you check out."],
   ["One question at a time", "Every question comes with three options. No walls of text."],
   ["Quiet hours", "No texts between 9 PM and 8 AM, and nothing on Sundays."],
   ["No secrets stored", "No passwords, no full account numbers. They can't sign in for you."],
   ["Everything is logged", "Every change has a name on it, so you can see who did what."],
  ],

